<%# Asks why before an action: Reject, Delete, Send Back and Restore on the
    review page, Hold on Fiscal. It sits inside the page's form, so the reason
    and the action are posted with the form itself. The button that opens it
    says what it posts -- data-value, a stable action name the controller
    dispatches on, never the button's text -- and data-commit, the label the
    submit button shows (aim_reason_controller). The reason goes into the
    invoice's history.
    `id` keeps the ids apart when a page holds two; `name` is the parameter
    the action is posted as (invoice_action on the review page), and `value`
    what a single-purpose dialog posts before anything opens it. %>
<% id = local_assigns.fetch(:id, 'aim-reason') %>
<div class="pb-modal-backdrop" data-aim-reason-target="backdrop" hidden>
  <div class="pb-modal" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="<%= id %>-title">
    <div class="pb-modal__header">
      <h3 id="<%= id %>-title" data-aim-reason-target="title"><%= local_assigns.fetch(:title, 'Why?') %></h3>
      <button type="button" class="pb-modal__close" data-action="aim-reason#close" aria-label="Close">✕</button>
    </div>
    <div class="pb-modal__body">
      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="<%= id %>-text">Reason</label>
        <textarea id="<%= id %>-text" name="reason" class="form-control" rows="3"
                  placeholder="<%= local_assigns.fetch(:placeholder, 'Briefly explain why') %>"
                  data-aim-reason-target="reason" disabled></textarea>
      </div>
      <div class="pb-modal__actions">
        <button type="button" class="btn" data-action="aim-reason#close">Cancel</button>
        <button type="submit" name="<%= local_assigns.fetch(:name, 'invoice_action') %>" value="<%= local_assigns[:value] %>"
                class="btn deny" data-aim-reason-target="submit"><%= local_assigns.fetch(:submit, 'Confirm') %></button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
